// darwin_pbpk/drugs/everolimus.sio — Everolimus PBPK Parameters
//
// Everolimus (Afinitor/Zortress, Novartis; Xience/Promus EES, Abbott) —
// sirolimus hydroxyethyl derivative, mTOR inhibitor, MW 958 Da.
// This file is the drug-identity home for the DES scenario: formulation,
// device load, release law, and systemic disposition accessors.
//
// Formulation modeled (SIO-524): XIENCE V everolimus-eluting stent,
// CoCr platform, durable fluoropolymer (PBMA/PVDF-HFP), 100 ug/cm^2,
// nominal load 37-181 ug by size. Canonical device: 3.0 x 18 mm,
// 0.088 mg everolimus (CIT 2008; Abhyankar TAXCO: 100 ug/cm^2 all sizes).
// Elution: ~80% by 30 days, remainder by ~4 months (SPIRIT FIRST;
// Thoracickey review; MBE 2017 modeling review: 80% within 30 days).
//
// Systemic disposition (oral labels, used for the systemic sink):
//   - substrate of CYP3A4 (+3A5, 2C8) and P-gp; parent is the main
//     circulating component (Afinitor SmPC; FDA Zortress label 2024)
//   - CL 8.8 L/h, Vd 110 L, t1/2 ~30 h (FDA label, transplant popPK n=673)
//   - oral F ~14-16% (not modeled: stent input goes to blood directly)
//   - Tmax 1-2 h oral (not modeled: no oral scenario here)
//
// Release law: Higuchi matrix diffusion Q(t) = KH*sqrt(t), fit to
// 80% at 720 h of the 0.088 mg load:
//   KH = 0.8 * 0.088 / sqrt(720) = 0.00262 mg/h^1/2.
// Singular at t = 0; both engines clip t < 0.1 h (Node core convention).
//
// Limitation (declared): arterial-wall concentration (the therapeutic
// compartment) is NOT modeled — systemic input only. Local fate and
// neointimal PD are SIO-524 follow-up.

pub fn everolimus_device_dose_mg() -> f64 { return 0.088 }
pub fn everolimus_kh_mg_per_sqrt_h() -> f64 { return 0.00262 }
pub fn everolimus_cl_L_per_h() -> f64 { return 8.8 }
